import IUT.Prerequisites.PadicLog
import IUT.PaperIV.Proposition1_2

/-!
# The p-adic logarithm on a finite extension of `ℚ_p`; IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (i)

Sources:
* Mochizuki, *Inter-universal Teichmüller Theory IV*, Proposition 1.2, pages 10 and 11, with the
  notation of Proposition 1.1 on page 9 (`ord` normalized by `ord(p) = 1`, `R_i` the ring of
  integers of a finite extension `k_i` of `ℚ_p`, `p ^ λ · R_i` the fractional ideal generated by
  an element of `ord` equal to `λ`). Page 10 defines, with `e_i` the ramification index of
  `k_i` over `ℚ_p`, `a_i = (1 / e_i) ⌈e_i / (p - 2)⌉` for `p > 2`, `a_i = 2` for `p = 2`, and
  `b_i = ⌊log (p e_i / (p - 1)) / log p⌋ - 1 / e_i`; assertion (i) is
  `p ^ (a_i) · R_i ⊆ log_p (R_i^×) ⊆ p ^ (-b_i) · R_i`, with equalities when `p > 2` and
  `e_i ≤ p - 2`. The proof on page 11 derives (i) from `a_i > 1 / (p - 1)` and
  `p ^ (b_i + 1 / e_i) / e_i > 1 / (p - 1)` and the theory of the `p`-adic logarithm and
  exponential ([Kobl], page 81).
* Mochizuki, *Inter-universal Teichmüller Theory III*, Definition 1.1, page 24 (the log-shell is
  the pre-log-shell, the image under the logarithm of the Galois-invariant units, multiplied by
  `(p*)⁻¹`, with `p* = p` for odd `p` and `p* = p ^ 2` for `p = 2`), and Proposition 1.2 (v),
  pages 31 and 32 ((a_non) compactness, (b_non) the log-shell contains the invariants of the
  integers, (c_non) it contains the image of the invariant units).

Pages read for this file: IUT IV pages 9, 10 and 11; IUT III pages 24, 31 and 32. Pages checked
against rendered images: the same.

## The model of the paper's objects

`K` is a normed field that is a normed `ℚ_p`-algebra (so its norm extends the `p`-adic norm,
`‖p‖ = 1 / p`, and `ord = -log_p ‖·‖`); for the results on units it is also complete and
locally compact (`ProperSpace`), which holds for every finite extension of `ℚ_p`
(`extLogUnit_image_bounds_of_finiteDimensional`). For a finite extension `L` given only by the
classes of `IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields.Padic` (`Field`, `Algebra ℚ_[p]`, `FiniteDimensional`), the
norm is Mathlib's spectral norm (`extLogUnit_image_bounds_spectralNorm`,
`extLogUnit_lower_and_shell_spectralNorm`). In this model:
* `R` is the closed unit ball `{‖x‖ ≤ 1}`, `R^×` the unit sphere `{‖x‖ = 1}`, and
  `p ^ λ · R` the closed ball `{‖z‖ ≤ p ^ (-λ)}`;
* `e` is a positive integer such that every `x` with `‖x‖ < 1` has `‖x‖ ^ e ≤ 1 / p`, that is
  `ord(x) ≥ 1 / e` on the maximal ideal (hypothesis `hval`). For the ramification index `e_i`
  this holds, since the value group of `k_i` is `p ^ (ℤ / e_i)`. It is a standing property of
  the field, not a claim of the paper; the results below hold for every such `e`;
* `log` on `R^×` is `extLogUnit`: `log u = N⁻¹ log (u ^ N)` where `N > 0` is any exponent with
  `‖u ^ N - 1‖ < 1` (the value does not depend on `N`, `extLogUnit_eq`) and `log (u ^ N)` is the
  series. Such `N` exist on `R^×` by local compactness (`extLog_exists_pow_near_one`), and the
  least one is prime to `p` (`extLog_find_not_dvd`). The pages read do not say how `log_p` is
  extended from the principal units to `R_i^×`; this is the standard extension (for `ℚ_p` it
  agrees with `IUT.Prerequisites.PadicLog.padicLogUnit`, `extLogUnit_padic`), and it is a
  homomorphism (`extLogUnit_mul`, `extLogUnit_pow`).

Not formalized: the identification of the closed unit ball with the ring of integers
`integralClosure ℤ_[p] k_i` used in `IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields.Padic`, of the unit sphere with its
units, and of the least `e` satisfying `hval` with `Ideal.ramificationIdx` of that file; the
uniqueness of the norm on `k_i`. The statements are therefore about the normed-field model
above, not about the objects of `Padic.lean`.

## Contents

1. The series in `K`: `extLogOnePlus x = ∑ (-1) ^ (n + 1) x ^ n / n`, convergent for `‖x‖ < 1`
   (`extLogSeries_summable`), equal to `NormedSpace.log (1 + x)`
   (`extLogOnePlus_eq_normedSpace_log`); the homomorphism property on the open unit disc
   (`extLogOnePlus_add_add_mul`, the double-series argument of `PadicLog.lean`); the isometry
   `‖log (1 + x)‖ = ‖x‖` on the disc `p ‖x‖ ^ (p - 1) < 1` (`extLogOnePlus_norm_eq`), which is the
   open disc of radius `p ^ (-1 / (p - 1))` (`extLog_mul_pow_lt_one_iff`). At the boundary
   `p ‖x‖ ^ (p - 1) = 1` the `p`-th term has the norm of the first
   (`extLogSeries_norm_eq_of_boundary`), so the radius is exact for the termwise estimate; that the isometry itself fails at the
   boundary in a suitable ramified field (`x = ζ_p - 1`) is not formalized.
2. In place of the exponential: on every closed ball of radius `r` with `p r ^ (p - 1) < 1`,
   `x ↦ log (1 + x)` is injective (`extLogOnePlus_injOn`, from the isometry of differences
   `extLogOnePlus_norm_sub_eq`) and maps the ball onto itself (`extLogOnePlus_image_closedBall`,
   surjectivity by the contraction mapping principle, `extLogOnePlus_surjOn`). The exponential
   series itself is not used.
3. IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (i) in the model above, with `a = Proposition1_2.a p e` and
   `b = Proposition1_2.b p e` (the constants of page 10, already in `Proposition1_2.lean`):
   `p ^ a · R ⊆ log (R^×)` (`extLogUnit_image_lower`, for every `e ≥ 1`, from
   `Proposition1_2.a_gt`), `log (R^×) ⊆ p ^ (-b) · R` (`extLogUnit_image_upper`, from
   `Proposition1_2.rpow_b_gt` and `hval`), both together (`extLogUnit_image_bounds`), the
   equality `log (R^×) = p ^ (1 / e) · R` for `p > 2`, `e ≤ p - 2`
   (`extLogUnit_image_eq_of_le`, with `Proposition1_2.a_b_of_le`), the unramified case
   `log (R^×) = p · R` for `p > 2` (`extLogUnit_image_unramified`), and consistency with the
   base field: for `K = ℚ_p` the image is `padicLogUnit_range_of_ne_two`'s
   (`extLogUnit_image_padic_of_ne_two`).
4. The log-shell `extLogShell p K = (p*)⁻¹ · log (R^×)` of IUT III Definition 1.1: it contains
   `R` (`extLogShell_unitBall_subset`, IUT III Proposition 1.2 (v) (b_non) in the model) and
   `log (R^×)` (`extLogUnit_image_subset_extLogShell`, (c_non)), and
   `p* p ^ a · R ⊆ I ⊆ p* p ^ (-b) · R` (`extLogShell_bounds`).

Not proved here: IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (ii) to (iv) (tensor products `R_I`, their
normalization, the automorphism `φ`, which rest on Proposition 1.1); the compactness (a_non) of
the log-shell; the link to `integralClosure` and `Ideal.ramificationIdx` described above.
-/

namespace IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields

open IUT.Prerequisites.PadicLog

section Series

variable {K : Type*} [NormedField K]

/-- The `n`-th term `(-1) ^ (n + 1) x ^ n / n` of the logarithm series in a normed field `K`; the
`0`-th term is `0` because `1 / 0 = 0`. -/
noncomputable def extLogSeries (x : K) (n : ℕ) : K :=
  (-1) ^ (n + 1) / n * x ^ n

/-- `log (1 + x) = ∑_{n ≥ 1} (-1) ^ (n + 1) x ^ n / n` in `K`; meaningful for `‖x‖ < 1` when `K`
is a complete normed `ℚ_p`-algebra (`extLogSeries_summable`), and a junk value otherwise. -/
noncomputable def extLogOnePlus (x : K) : K :=
  ∑' n : ℕ, extLogSeries x n

/-- `log 1 = 0`. -/
theorem extLogOnePlus_zero : extLogOnePlus (0 : K) = 0 := by
  rw [extLogOnePlus]
  convert tsum_zero with n
  rcases n with _ | n <;> simp [extLogSeries]

/-- The double family used to re-expand `log (1 + x + w)` around `x`. -/
noncomputable def extLogDouble (x w : K) (nk : ℕ × ℕ) : K :=
  (-1) ^ (nk.1 + 1) / nk.1 * (nk.1.choose nk.2) * x ^ (nk.1 - nk.2) * w ^ nk.2

/-- Summing the double family over `k` first gives the series of `log (1 + (x + w))`. -/
theorem extLogDouble_hasSum_fst (x w : K) (n : ℕ) :
    HasSum (fun k => extLogDouble x w (n, k)) (extLogSeries (x + w) n) := by
  have hzero : ∀ k ∉ Finset.range (n + 1), extLogDouble x w (n, k) = 0 := by
    intro k hk
    simp only [Finset.mem_range, not_lt] at hk
    simp [extLogDouble, Nat.choose_eq_zero_of_lt (by omega : n < k)]
  convert hasSum_sum_of_ne_finset_zero hzero using 1
  swap; · infer_instance
  rw [extLogSeries, add_comm x w, add_pow, Finset.mul_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ => ?_
  simp only [extLogDouble]
  ring

/-- The ultrametric inequality for a difference. -/
theorem extLog_norm_sub_le_max [IsUltrametricDist K] (u v : K) : ‖u - v‖ ≤ max ‖u‖ ‖v‖ := by
  simpa [sub_eq_add_neg] using IsUltrametricDist.norm_add_le_max u (-v)

/-- `‖1 + x‖ = 1` for `‖x‖ < 1` in an ultrametric normed field. -/
theorem extLog_norm_one_add [IsUltrametricDist K] {x : K} (hx : ‖x‖ < 1) : ‖1 + x‖ = 1 := by
  rw [IsUltrametricDist.norm_add_eq_max_of_norm_ne_norm (by rw [norm_one]; exact hx.ne'),
    norm_one, max_eq_left hx.le]

/-- If `p t ^ (p - 1) < 1` for a natural number `p ≥ 1`, then `t < 1`. -/
theorem extLog_lt_one_of_mul_pow_lt_one {p : ℕ} (hp : 1 ≤ p) {t : ℝ}
    (h : (p : ℝ) * t ^ (p - 1) < 1) : t < 1 := by
  by_contra hc
  replace hc := not_lt.mp hc
  have h1 : 1 ≤ t ^ (p - 1) := one_le_pow₀ hc
  have hp' : (1 : ℝ) ≤ p := by exact_mod_cast hp
  nlinarith

end Series

section Arith

/-- Bernoulli's inequality in `ℕ`: `1 + v (p - 1) ≤ p ^ v` for `p ≥ 1`. -/
theorem extLog_one_add_mul_le_pow {p : ℕ} (hp : 1 ≤ p) (v : ℕ) : 1 + v * (p - 1) ≤ p ^ v := by
  obtain ⟨q, rfl⟩ : ∃ q, p = q + 1 := ⟨p - 1, by omega⟩
  simp only [Nat.add_sub_cancel]
  induction v with
  | zero => simp
  | succ v ih =>
    rw [pow_succ]
    have h1 := Nat.mul_le_mul_right (q + 1) ih
    have h2 : (1 + v * q) * (q + 1) = 1 + (v + 1) * q + v * q * q := by ring
    omega

/-- The arithmetic behind the upper bound of IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (i): if `p ≥ 2`,
`e < p ^ (c + 1)`, `n ≥ 1` and `p ^ v ≤ n`, then `v e ≤ c e + (n - 1)`. -/
theorem extLog_val_arith {p e c v n : ℕ} (hp : 2 ≤ p) (hn : 1 ≤ n) (hpv : p ^ v ≤ n)
    (he : e < p ^ (c + 1)) : v * e ≤ c * e + (n - 1) := by
  rcases le_or_gt v c with hvc | hvc
  · have := Nat.mul_le_mul_right e hvc
    omega
  obtain ⟨j, rfl⟩ : ∃ j, v = c + 1 + j := ⟨v - (c + 1), by omega⟩
  have h1 : 1 + j ≤ p ^ j := by
    have := extLog_one_add_mul_le_pow (by omega : 1 ≤ p) j
    have : j ≤ j * (p - 1) := Nat.le_mul_of_pos_right j (by omega)
    omega
  have h2 : (e + 1) * (1 + j) ≤ p ^ (c + 1 + j) := by
    rw [pow_add]
    exact Nat.mul_le_mul (by omega) h1
  have h3 : (c + 1 + j) * e = c * e + (1 + j) * e := by ring
  rw [h3]
  have h4 : (e + 1) * (1 + j) = (1 + j) * e + (1 + j) := by ring
  omega

end Arith

section General

variable (p : ℕ) [hp : Fact p.Prime] {K : Type*} [NormedField K] [NormedAlgebra ℚ_[p] K]

include hp

/-- The norm of a natural number in a normed `ℚ_p`-algebra is its `p`-adic norm. -/
theorem extLog_norm_natCast (n : ℕ) : ‖(n : K)‖ = ‖(n : ℚ_[p])‖ := by
  rw [← map_natCast (algebraMap ℚ_[p] K) n, norm_algebraMap']

/-- A normed field that is a normed `ℚ_p`-algebra is ultrametric. -/
theorem extLog_isUltrametricDist : IsUltrametricDist K :=
  IsUltrametricDist.of_normedAlgebra ℚ_[p]

/-- A normed field that is a normed `ℚ_p`-algebra has characteristic zero. -/
theorem extLog_charZero : CharZero K :=
  charZero_of_injective_algebraMap (algebraMap ℚ_[p] K).injective

/-- `‖1 / n‖ ≤ n` in `K`. -/
theorem extLog_norm_inv_natCast_le (n : ℕ) : ‖(n : K)⁻¹‖ ≤ n := by
  rw [norm_inv, extLog_norm_natCast p, ← norm_inv]
  exact padicLog_norm_inv_natCast_le (p := p) n

/-- `‖n‖ ≤ 1` in `K`. -/
theorem extLog_norm_natCast_le_one (n : ℕ) : ‖(n : K)‖ ≤ 1 := by
  rw [extLog_norm_natCast p]
  simpa using Padic.norm_int_le_one (p := p) (n : ℤ)

/-- `‖x ^ n / n‖ ≤ n ‖x‖ ^ n`. -/
theorem extLogSeries_norm_le (x : K) (n : ℕ) : ‖extLogSeries x n‖ ≤ n * ‖x‖ ^ n := by
  rw [extLogSeries, div_eq_mul_inv, norm_mul, norm_mul, norm_pow, norm_neg, norm_one, one_pow,
    one_mul, norm_pow]
  exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (extLog_norm_inv_natCast_le p n) (by positivity)

/-- The logarithm series converges on the open unit disc of a complete normed `ℚ_p`-algebra. -/
theorem extLogSeries_summable [CompleteSpace K] {x : K} (hx : ‖x‖ < 1) :
    Summable (extLogSeries x) := by
  refine Summable.of_norm_bounded (g := fun n : ℕ => (n : ℝ) ^ 1 * ‖x‖ ^ n) ?_ ?_
  · exact summable_pow_mul_geometric_of_norm_lt_one 1 (by simpa using hx)
  · intro n; simpa using extLogSeries_norm_le p x n

/-- Agreement with Mathlib's `NormedSpace.log`. -/
theorem extLogOnePlus_eq_normedSpace_log (x : K) :
    extLogOnePlus x = NormedSpace.log (1 + x) := by
  have := extLog_charZero p (K := K)
  rw [NormedSpace.log_eq_tsum K]
  simp [extLogOnePlus, extLogSeries, smul_eq_mul]

/-- `log (1 + x) = x + ∑_{n ≥ 2} (-1) ^ (n + 1) x ^ n / n` for `‖x‖ < 1`. -/
theorem extLogOnePlus_eq_add_tail [CompleteSpace K] {x : K} (hx : ‖x‖ < 1) :
    extLogOnePlus x = x + ∑' n : ℕ, extLogSeries x (n + 2) := by
  rw [extLogOnePlus, ← (extLogSeries_summable p hx).sum_add_tsum_nat_add 2]
  simp [Finset.sum_range_succ, extLogSeries]

/-- The key term estimate: for `n ≥ 2`, `0 ≤ r ≤ 1`, `p r ^ (p - 1) ≤ 1` and `‖x‖ ≤ r`,
`‖x ^ n / n‖ ≤ max (p r ^ (p - 1)) r · ‖x‖`. -/
theorem extLogSeries_norm_le_max {r : ℝ} (hr1 : r ≤ 1) (hpr : (p : ℝ) * r ^ (p - 1) ≤ 1)
    {x : K} (hx : ‖x‖ ≤ r) {n : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) :
    ‖extLogSeries x n‖ ≤ max ((p : ℝ) * r ^ (p - 1)) r * ‖x‖ := by
  obtain ⟨v, hdvd, hv⟩ := padicLog_exists_norm_inv_natCast (p := p) (n := n) (by omega)
  have hr0 : 0 ≤ r := (norm_nonneg x).trans hx
  have hp0 : (0 : ℝ) ≤ p := by positivity
  rw [extLogSeries, div_eq_mul_inv, norm_mul, norm_mul, norm_pow, norm_neg, norm_one, one_pow,
    one_mul, norm_pow, norm_inv, extLog_norm_natCast p, ← norm_inv, hv]
  obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ : ∃ m, n = m + 1 := ⟨n - 1, by omega⟩
  rw [pow_succ]
  have hxm : ‖x‖ ^ m ≤ r ^ m := pow_le_pow_left₀ (norm_nonneg _) hx m
  suffices h : (p : ℝ) ^ v * r ^ m ≤ max ((p : ℝ) * r ^ (p - 1)) r by
    calc (p : ℝ) ^ v * (‖x‖ ^ m * ‖x‖) = ((p : ℝ) ^ v * ‖x‖ ^ m) * ‖x‖ := by ring
      _ ≤ ((p : ℝ) ^ v * r ^ m) * ‖x‖ := by gcongr
      _ ≤ _ := by gcongr
  rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos v with rfl | hv0
  · rw [pow_zero, one_mul]
    exact le_max_of_le_right (pow_le_of_le_one hr0 hr1 (by omega))
  · have hle : p ^ v ≤ m + 1 := Nat.le_of_dvd (by omega) hdvd
    have hb := extLog_one_add_mul_le_pow hp.out.one_lt.le v
    have hvm : v * (p - 1) ≤ m := by omega
    have h1 : r ^ m ≤ r ^ (v * (p - 1)) := pow_le_pow_of_le_one hr0 hr1 hvm
    have h2 : (p : ℝ) ^ v * r ^ (v * (p - 1)) = ((p : ℝ) * r ^ (p - 1)) ^ v := by
      rw [mul_pow, ← pow_mul, mul_comm (p - 1) v]
    refine le_max_of_le_left ?_
    calc (p : ℝ) ^ v * r ^ m ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ v * r ^ (v * (p - 1)) := by gcongr
      _ = ((p : ℝ) * r ^ (p - 1)) ^ v := h2
      _ ≤ (p : ℝ) * r ^ (p - 1) := pow_le_of_le_one (by positivity) hpr (by omega)

/-- The tail `∑_{n ≥ 2}` of the series is bounded by `max (p r ^ (p - 1)) r · ‖x‖` for
`‖x‖ ≤ r`, `p r ^ (p - 1) < 1`. -/
theorem extLog_tail_norm_le {r : ℝ} (hr0 : 0 ≤ r) (hpr : (p : ℝ) * r ^ (p - 1) < 1) {x : K}
    (hx : ‖x‖ ≤ r) :
    ‖∑' n : ℕ, extLogSeries x (n + 2)‖ ≤ max ((p : ℝ) * r ^ (p - 1)) r * ‖x‖ := by
  have := extLog_isUltrametricDist p (K := K)
  have hr1 := extLog_lt_one_of_mul_pow_lt_one hp.out.one_lt.le hpr
  exact IsUltrametricDist.norm_tsum_le_of_forall_le_of_nonneg
    (mul_nonneg (le_max_of_le_right hr0) (norm_nonneg _))
    fun n => extLogSeries_norm_le_max p hr1.le hpr.le hx (by omega)

/-- **Isometry**: `‖log (1 + x)‖ = ‖x‖` on the disc `p ‖x‖ ^ (p - 1) < 1`, that is
`‖x‖ < p ^ (-1 / (p - 1))` (`extLog_mul_pow_lt_one_iff`). -/
theorem extLogOnePlus_norm_eq [CompleteSpace K] {x : K} (hx : (p : ℝ) * ‖x‖ ^ (p - 1) < 1) :
    ‖extLogOnePlus x‖ = ‖x‖ := by
  have := extLog_isUltrametricDist p (K := K)
  have hx1 := extLog_lt_one_of_mul_pow_lt_one hp.out.one_lt.le hx
  rcases eq_or_ne x 0 with rfl | hx0
  · simp [extLogOnePlus_zero]
  have hpos : 0 < ‖x‖ := norm_pos_iff.mpr hx0
  have htail := extLog_tail_norm_le p (norm_nonneg x) hx le_rfl
  have hlt : ‖∑' n : ℕ, extLogSeries x (n + 2)‖ < ‖x‖ :=
    htail.trans_lt (mul_lt_of_lt_one_left hpos (max_lt hx hx1))
  rw [extLogOnePlus_eq_add_tail p hx1,
    IsUltrametricDist.norm_add_eq_max_of_norm_ne_norm hlt.ne', max_eq_left hlt.le]

/-- The disc of the isometry is the open disc of radius `p ^ (-1 / (p - 1))`. -/
theorem extLog_mul_pow_lt_one_iff {t : ℝ} (ht : 0 ≤ t) :
    (p : ℝ) * t ^ (p - 1) < 1 ↔ t < (p : ℝ) ^ (-(1 / ((p : ℝ) - 1))) := by
  have hp2 := hp.out.two_le
  have hp0 : (0 : ℝ) < p := by exact_mod_cast hp.out.pos
  have hs : ((p - 1 : ℕ) : ℝ) = (p : ℝ) - 1 := by
    rw [Nat.cast_sub (by omega)]; simp
  have hs0 : (0 : ℝ) < (p : ℝ) - 1 := by
    have : (2 : ℝ) ≤ p := by exact_mod_cast hp2
    linarith
  have hpow : ((p : ℝ) ^ (-(1 / ((p : ℝ) - 1)))) ^ (p - 1) = (p : ℝ)⁻¹ := by
    rw [← Real.rpow_natCast, ← Real.rpow_mul hp0.le, hs,
      show -(1 / ((p : ℝ) - 1)) * ((p : ℝ) - 1) = -1 by field_simp, Real.rpow_neg_one]
  rw [← pow_lt_pow_iff_left₀ ht (Real.rpow_nonneg hp0.le _) (by omega : p - 1 ≠ 0), hpow,
    ← one_div, lt_div_iff₀' hp0]

/-- At the boundary `p ‖x‖ ^ (p - 1) = 1` of the disc, the `p`-th term has the same norm as the
first: the termwise estimate behind `extLogOnePlus_norm_eq` fails there, so the radius
`p ^ (-1 / (p - 1))` is the exact radius of that estimate. -/
theorem extLogSeries_norm_eq_of_boundary {x : K} (hx : (p : ℝ) * ‖x‖ ^ (p - 1) = 1) :
    ‖extLogSeries x p‖ = ‖x‖ := by
  rw [extLogSeries, div_eq_mul_inv, norm_mul, norm_mul, norm_pow, norm_neg, norm_one, one_pow,
    one_mul, norm_pow, norm_inv, extLog_norm_natCast p, Padic.norm_p, inv_inv]
  calc (p : ℝ) * ‖x‖ ^ p = ((p : ℝ) * ‖x‖ ^ (p - 1)) * ‖x‖ := by
        rw [mul_assoc, ← pow_succ, Nat.sub_add_cancel hp.out.one_lt.le]
    _ = ‖x‖ := by rw [hx, one_mul]

/-- The double family is norm-summable for `‖x‖, ‖w‖ < 1`. -/
theorem extLogDouble_summable [CompleteSpace K] {x w : K} (hx : ‖x‖ < 1) (hw : ‖w‖ < 1) :
    Summable (extLogDouble x w) := by
  set r := max ‖x‖ ‖w‖
  have hr0 : 0 ≤ r := le_max_of_le_left (norm_nonneg _)
  have hr1 : r < 1 := max_lt hx hw
  set s := Real.sqrt r
  have hs0 : 0 ≤ s := Real.sqrt_nonneg _
  have hs1 : s < 1 := (Real.sqrt_lt' one_pos).mpr (by simpa using hr1)
  have hss : s * s = r := Real.mul_self_sqrt hr0
  refine Summable.of_norm_bounded
    (g := fun nk : ℕ × ℕ => ((nk.1 : ℝ) ^ 1 * s ^ nk.1) * s ^ nk.2) ?_ ?_
  · refine Summable.mul_of_nonneg (f := fun n : ℕ => (n : ℝ) ^ 1 * s ^ n) (g := fun k => s ^ k)
      (summable_pow_mul_geometric_of_norm_lt_one 1 (by rwa [Real.norm_of_nonneg hs0]))
      (summable_geometric_of_lt_one hs0 hs1) (fun n => by positivity) (fun k => by positivity)
  · rintro ⟨n, k⟩
    simp only [extLogDouble, pow_one]
    rcases lt_or_ge n k with hnk | hkn
    · simp [Nat.choose_eq_zero_of_lt hnk]; positivity
    rw [div_eq_mul_inv, norm_mul, norm_mul, norm_mul, norm_mul, norm_pow, norm_neg, norm_one,
      one_pow, one_mul, norm_pow, norm_pow]
    have hc : ‖((n.choose k : ℕ) : K)‖ ≤ 1 := extLog_norm_natCast_le_one p _
    have h1 : ‖x‖ ^ (n - k) * ‖w‖ ^ k ≤ s ^ n * s ^ k := by
      have : ‖x‖ ^ (n - k) * ‖w‖ ^ k ≤ r ^ (n - k) * r ^ k := by
        gcongr
        · exact le_max_left _ _
        · exact le_max_right _ _
      calc ‖x‖ ^ (n - k) * ‖w‖ ^ k ≤ r ^ (n - k) * r ^ k := this
        _ = r ^ n := by rw [← pow_add, Nat.sub_add_cancel hkn]
        _ = s ^ n * s ^ n := by rw [← mul_pow, hss]
        _ ≤ s ^ n * s ^ k :=
            mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (pow_le_pow_of_le_one hs0 hs1.le hkn) (by positivity)
    calc ‖((n : K))⁻¹‖ * ‖((n.choose k : ℕ) : K)‖ * ‖x‖ ^ (n - k) * ‖w‖ ^ k
        ≤ n * 1 * (‖x‖ ^ (n - k) * ‖w‖ ^ k) := by
          rw [mul_assoc _ (‖x‖ ^ _)]
          gcongr
          exact extLog_norm_inv_natCast_le p n
      _ ≤ n * 1 * (s ^ n * s ^ k) := by gcongr
      _ = n * s ^ n * s ^ k := by ring

/-- Summing the double family over `n` first, for fixed `k ≥ 1`. -/
theorem extLogDouble_hasSum_snd_succ [CompleteSpace K] {x : K} (hx : ‖x‖ < 1) (w : K) (j : ℕ) :
    HasSum (fun n => extLogDouble x w (n, j + 1))
      ((-1) ^ (j + 2) / (j + 1 : ℕ) * (w / (1 + x)) ^ (j + 1)) := by
  have := extLog_charZero p (K := K)
  have hx' : ‖-x‖ < 1 := by rwa [norm_neg]
  have h1x : (1 + x) ≠ 0 := by
    intro h
    have : x = -1 := by linear_combination h
    rw [this, norm_neg, norm_one] at hx
    exact lt_irrefl _ hx
  have hgeom := (hasSum_choose_mul_geometric_of_norm_lt_one (𝕜 := K) j hx').mul_left
    ((-1) ^ j / (j + 1 : ℕ) * w ^ (j + 1))
  rw [← hasSum_nat_add_iff' (j + 1)]
  have hlow : ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (j + 1), extLogDouble x w (i, j + 1) = 0 := by
    refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun i hi => ?_
    simp only [Finset.mem_range] at hi
    simp [extLogDouble, Nat.choose_eq_zero_of_lt hi]
  rw [hlow, sub_zero]
  convert hgeom using 1
  · funext m
    simp only [extLogDouble]
    have hc : ((m + (j + 1)).choose (j + 1) : K) * (j + 1 : ℕ) =
        (m + j + 1 : ℕ) * ((m + j).choose j : ℕ) := by
      have := Nat.add_one_mul_choose_eq (m + j) j
      rw [show m + (j + 1) = m + j + 1 by omega]
      exact_mod_cast this.symm
    have hj : ((j + 1 : ℕ) : K) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast Nat.succ_ne_zero j
    have hmj : ((m + (j + 1) : ℕ) : K) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast (by omega : m + (j + 1) ≠ 0)
    rw [show m + (j + 1) - (j + 1) = m by omega]
    field_simp
    rw [show ((m + (j + 1) : ℕ) : K) = ((m + j + 1 : ℕ) : K) by push_cast; ring] at hmj ⊢
    rw [show (-1 : K) ^ (m + (j + 1) + 1) * ((m + (j + 1)).choose (j + 1) : ℕ) * x ^ m *
        w ^ (j + 1) * ((j + 1 : ℕ) : K) = (-1) ^ (m + j) * x ^ m * w ^ (j + 1) *
        ((((m + (j + 1)).choose (j + 1) : ℕ) : K) * ((j + 1 : ℕ) : K)) by ring, hc]
    ring
  · rw [sub_neg_eq_add, div_pow]
    field_simp
    ring

/-- **Homomorphism property** on the open unit disc of a complete normed `ℚ_p`-algebra:
`log ((1 + x) (1 + y)) = log (1 + x) + log (1 + y)` for `‖x‖, ‖y‖ < 1`. -/
theorem extLogOnePlus_add_add_mul [CompleteSpace K] {x y : K} (hx : ‖x‖ < 1) (hy : ‖y‖ < 1) :
    extLogOnePlus (x + y + x * y) = extLogOnePlus x + extLogOnePlus y := by
  have := extLog_isUltrametricDist p (K := K)
  set w := (1 + x) * y with hwdef
  have h1x := extLog_norm_one_add hx
  have hw : ‖w‖ < 1 := by rw [hwdef, norm_mul, h1x, one_mul]; exact hy
  have hxw : x + y + x * y = x + w := by rw [hwdef]; ring
  have hS := (extLogDouble_summable p hx hw).hasSum
  have hfst : HasSum (extLogSeries (x + w)) (∑' nk, extLogDouble x w nk) :=
    hS.prod_fiberwise (extLogDouble_hasSum_fst x w)
  have hswap := (Equiv.prodComm ℕ ℕ).hasSum_iff.mpr hS
  have h1x0 : (1 + x) ≠ 0 := by
    intro h; rw [h, norm_zero] at h1x; exact zero_ne_one h1x
  have hsnd : HasSum (fun k => extLogSeries y k + if k = 0 then extLogOnePlus x else 0)
      (∑' nk, extLogDouble x w nk) := by
    refine hswap.prod_fiberwise fun k => ?_
    rcases k with _ | j
    · simp only [Function.comp_apply, Equiv.prodComm_apply, Prod.swap_prod_mk, ite_true]
      have : extLogSeries y 0 = 0 := by simp [extLogSeries]
      rw [this, zero_add, extLogOnePlus]
      convert (extLogSeries_summable p hx).hasSum using 1
      funext n
      simp [extLogDouble, extLogSeries]
    · simp only [Function.comp_apply, Equiv.prodComm_apply, Prod.swap_prod_mk,
        show j + 1 ≠ 0 from Nat.succ_ne_zero j, ite_false, add_zero]
      convert extLogDouble_hasSum_snd_succ p hx w j using 1
      rw [hwdef, mul_div_cancel_left₀ _ h1x0, extLogSeries]
  have hsnd' : HasSum (fun k => extLogSeries y k + if k = 0 then extLogOnePlus x else 0)
      (extLogOnePlus y + extLogOnePlus x) :=
    (extLogSeries_summable p hy).hasSum.add (hasSum_ite_eq 0 _)
  rw [hxw, extLogOnePlus, hfst.tsum_eq, hsnd.unique hsnd', add_comm]

/-- `log ((1 + x) ^ n) = n log (1 + x)` on the open unit disc. -/
theorem extLogOnePlus_pow_sub_one [CompleteSpace K] {x : K} (hx : ‖x‖ < 1) (n : ℕ) :
    ‖(1 + x) ^ n - 1‖ < 1 ∧ extLogOnePlus ((1 + x) ^ n - 1) = n * extLogOnePlus x := by
  have := extLog_isUltrametricDist p (K := K)
  induction n with
  | zero => simp [extLogOnePlus_zero]
  | succ n ih =>
    obtain ⟨hy, hL⟩ := ih
    have he : (1 + x) ^ (n + 1) - 1 = ((1 + x) ^ n - 1) + x + ((1 + x) ^ n - 1) * x := by ring
    refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [he]
      refine (IsUltrametricDist.norm_add_le_max _ _).trans_lt (max_lt ?_ ?_)
      · exact (IsUltrametricDist.norm_add_le_max _ _).trans_lt (max_lt hy hx)
      · rw [norm_mul]; exact (mul_le_of_le_one_right (norm_nonneg _) hx.le).trans_lt hy
    · rw [he, extLogOnePlus_add_add_mul p hy hx, hL]; push_cast; ring

/-- `log (1 + a) - log (1 + b) = log (1 + c)` with `c = (a - b) / (1 + b)`, for `‖a‖, ‖b‖ < 1`. -/
theorem extLogOnePlus_sub_eq [CompleteSpace K] {a b : K} (ha : ‖a‖ < 1) (hb : ‖b‖ < 1) :
    ‖(a - b) / (1 + b)‖ = ‖a - b‖ ∧
      extLogOnePlus a - extLogOnePlus b = extLogOnePlus ((a - b) / (1 + b)) := by
  have := extLog_isUltrametricDist p (K := K)
  have h1b := extLog_norm_one_add hb
  have h1b0 : (1 + b) ≠ 0 := by intro h; rw [h, norm_zero] at h1b; exact zero_ne_one h1b
  have hc : ‖(a - b) / (1 + b)‖ = ‖a - b‖ := by rw [norm_div, h1b, div_one]
  have hc1 : ‖(a - b) / (1 + b)‖ < 1 :=
    hc ▸ (extLog_norm_sub_le_max a b).trans_lt (max_lt ha hb)
  have habc : b + (a - b) / (1 + b) + b * ((a - b) / (1 + b)) = a := by field_simp; ring
  refine ⟨hc, ?_⟩
  have h := extLogOnePlus_add_add_mul p hb hc1
  rw [habc] at h
  rw [h]
  ring

/-- **Isometry of differences**: `‖log (1 + a) - log (1 + b)‖ = ‖a - b‖` on the disc
`p ‖·‖ ^ (p - 1) < 1`; in particular `x ↦ log (1 + x)` is injective there. -/
theorem extLogOnePlus_norm_sub_eq [CompleteSpace K] {a b : K}
    (ha : (p : ℝ) * ‖a‖ ^ (p - 1) < 1) (hb : (p : ℝ) * ‖b‖ ^ (p - 1) < 1) :
    ‖extLogOnePlus a - extLogOnePlus b‖ = ‖a - b‖ := by
  have := extLog_isUltrametricDist p (K := K)
  have ha1 := extLog_lt_one_of_mul_pow_lt_one hp.out.one_lt.le ha
  have hb1 := extLog_lt_one_of_mul_pow_lt_one hp.out.one_lt.le hb
  obtain ⟨hc, hL⟩ := extLogOnePlus_sub_eq p ha1 hb1
  have hcd : (p : ℝ) * ‖(a - b) / (1 + b)‖ ^ (p - 1) < 1 := by
    rw [hc]
    have hm : ‖a - b‖ ≤ max ‖a‖ ‖b‖ := extLog_norm_sub_le_max a b
    have hmax : (p : ℝ) * (max ‖a‖ ‖b‖) ^ (p - 1) < 1 := by
      rcases le_total ‖a‖ ‖b‖ with h | h
      · rw [max_eq_right h]; exact hb
      · rw [max_eq_left h]; exact ha
    calc (p : ℝ) * ‖a - b‖ ^ (p - 1) ≤ (p : ℝ) * (max ‖a‖ ‖b‖) ^ (p - 1) := by gcongr
      _ < 1 := hmax
  rw [hL, extLogOnePlus_norm_eq p hcd, hc]

/-- Injectivity of `x ↦ log (1 + x)` on the disc `p ‖x‖ ^ (p - 1) < 1`. -/
theorem extLogOnePlus_injOn [CompleteSpace K] :
    Set.InjOn (extLogOnePlus (K := K)) {x : K | (p : ℝ) * ‖x‖ ^ (p - 1) < 1} := by
  intro a ha b hb hab
  have h := extLogOnePlus_norm_sub_eq p ha hb
  rw [hab, sub_self, norm_zero] at h
  exact sub_eq_zero.mp (norm_eq_zero.mp h.symm)

/-- Contraction estimate: for `a, b` in the closed ball of radius `r`, `p r ^ (p - 1) < 1`,
`‖(a - b) - (log (1 + a) - log (1 + b))‖ ≤ max (p r ^ (p - 1)) r · ‖a - b‖`. -/
theorem extLogOnePlus_sub_sub_norm_le [CompleteSpace K] {r : ℝ} (hr0 : 0 ≤ r)
    (hpr : (p : ℝ) * r ^ (p - 1) < 1) {a b : K} (ha : ‖a‖ ≤ r) (hb : ‖b‖ ≤ r) :
    ‖(a - b) - (extLogOnePlus a - extLogOnePlus b)‖ ≤
      max ((p : ℝ) * r ^ (p - 1)) r * ‖a - b‖ := by
  have := extLog_isUltrametricDist p (K := K)
  have hr1 := extLog_lt_one_of_mul_pow_lt_one hp.out.one_lt.le hpr
  have hb1 : ‖b‖ < 1 := hb.trans_lt hr1
  have ha1 : ‖a‖ < 1 := ha.trans_lt hr1
  have h1b := extLog_norm_one_add hb1
  have h1b0 : (1 + b) ≠ 0 := by intro h; rw [h, norm_zero] at h1b; exact zero_ne_one h1b
  obtain ⟨hc, hL⟩ := extLogOnePlus_sub_eq p ha1 hb1
  set c := (a - b) / (1 + b) with hcdef
  have hcr : ‖c‖ ≤ r := by
    rw [hc]; exact (extLog_norm_sub_le_max a b).trans (max_le ha hb)
  have hc1 : ‖c‖ < 1 := hcr.trans_lt hr1
  have hab : a - b = c + c * b := by rw [hcdef]; field_simp
  have htail := extLog_tail_norm_le p hr0 hpr hcr
  have hcb : ‖c * b‖ ≤ max ((p : ℝ) * r ^ (p - 1)) r * ‖c‖ := by
    rw [norm_mul, mul_comm]
    exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (hb.trans (le_max_right _ _)) (norm_nonneg _)
  rw [hL, extLogOnePlus_eq_add_tail p hc1, ← hc, hab,
    show c + c * b - (c + ∑' n : ℕ, extLogSeries c (n + 2)) =
      c * b - ∑' n : ℕ, extLogSeries c (n + 2) by ring]
  exact (extLog_norm_sub_le_max _ _).trans (max_le hcb htail)

/-- **Surjectivity** of `x ↦ log (1 + x)` onto the closed ball of radius `r`, for
`p r ^ (p - 1) < 1`, by the contraction mapping principle. -/
theorem extLogOnePlus_surjOn [CompleteSpace K] {r : ℝ} (hr0 : 0 ≤ r)
    (hpr : (p : ℝ) * r ^ (p - 1) < 1) {z : K} (hz : ‖z‖ ≤ r) :
    ∃ x : K, ‖x‖ ≤ r ∧ extLogOnePlus x = z := by
  have := extLog_isUltrametricDist p (K := K)
  set B := Metric.closedBall (0 : K) r
  have hr1 := extLog_lt_one_of_mul_pow_lt_one hp.out.one_lt.le hpr
  set M : ℝ := max ((p : ℝ) * r ^ (p - 1)) r with hMdef
  have hM0 : 0 ≤ M := le_max_of_le_right hr0
  have hM1 : M < 1 := max_lt hpr hr1
  have hmem : ∀ x : B, x.1 + (z - extLogOnePlus x.1) ∈ B := by
    intro ⟨x, hx⟩
    rw [Metric.mem_closedBall, dist_zero_right] at hx ⊢
    have hx1 : ‖x‖ < 1 := hx.trans_lt hr1
    have htail := extLog_tail_norm_le p hr0 hpr hx
    rw [extLogOnePlus_eq_add_tail p hx1,
      show x + (z - (x + ∑' n : ℕ, extLogSeries x (n + 2))) =
        z - ∑' n : ℕ, extLogSeries x (n + 2) by ring]
    refine (extLog_norm_sub_le_max _ _).trans (max_le hz (htail.trans ?_))
    calc M * ‖x‖ ≤ 1 * ‖x‖ := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right hM1.le (norm_nonneg _)
      _ = ‖x‖ := one_mul _
      _ ≤ r := hx
  let T : B → B := fun x => ⟨x.1 + (z - extLogOnePlus x.1), hmem x⟩
  let Mn : NNReal := ⟨M, hM0⟩
  have hT : ContractingWith Mn T := by
    refine ⟨?_, LipschitzWith.of_dist_le_mul fun a b => ?_⟩
    · rw [← NNReal.coe_lt_coe, NNReal.coe_one]; exact hM1
    · rw [Subtype.dist_eq, Subtype.dist_eq, dist_eq_norm, dist_eq_norm]
      have ha := a.2; have hb := b.2
      rw [Metric.mem_closedBall, dist_zero_right] at ha hb
      have := extLogOnePlus_sub_sub_norm_le p hr0 hpr ha hb
      simp only [T]
      rw [show a.1 + (z - extLogOnePlus a.1) - (b.1 + (z - extLogOnePlus b.1)) =
        (a.1 - b.1) - (extLogOnePlus a.1 - extLogOnePlus b.1) by ring]
      exact this
  have : CompleteSpace B := Metric.isClosed_closedBall.completeSpace_coe
  have : Nonempty B := ⟨⟨0, Metric.mem_closedBall_self hr0⟩⟩
  set x := ContractingWith.fixedPoint T hT
  have hfix : T x = x := ContractingWith.fixedPoint_isFixedPt hT
  have hx := x.2
  rw [Metric.mem_closedBall, dist_zero_right] at hx
  refine ⟨x.1, hx, ?_⟩
  have := congrArg Subtype.val hfix
  simp only [T] at this
  linear_combination -this

/-- `x ↦ log (1 + x)` maps the closed ball of radius `r` onto itself when `p r ^ (p - 1) < 1`
(and is injective there, `extLogOnePlus_injOn`). -/
theorem extLogOnePlus_image_closedBall [CompleteSpace K] {r : ℝ} (hr0 : 0 ≤ r)
    (hpr : (p : ℝ) * r ^ (p - 1) < 1) :
    extLogOnePlus '' {x : K | ‖x‖ ≤ r} = {z : K | ‖z‖ ≤ r} := by
  ext z
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    have hx' : (p : ℝ) * ‖x‖ ^ (p - 1) < 1 :=
      lt_of_le_of_lt (by gcongr; exact hx) hpr
    show ‖extLogOnePlus x‖ ≤ r
    rw [extLogOnePlus_norm_eq p hx']; exact hx
  · intro hz
    obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := extLogOnePlus_surjOn p hr0 hpr hz
    exact ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩

end General

section Units

open Classical in
/-- The logarithm of an element `u` of `K` some positive power of which lies in the open unit disc
around `1`: `log u = N⁻¹ log (u ^ N)` with `N` the least positive such exponent, where
`log (u ^ N)` is the series `extLogOnePlus (u ^ N - 1)`. The value does not depend on the
choice of `N` (`extLogUnit_eq`), and on the units of a locally compact `K` such an `N` exists
(`extLog_exists_pow_near_one`). Junk value `0` if there is no such `N`. -/
noncomputable def extLogUnit {K : Type*} [NormedField K] (u : K) : K :=
  if h : ∃ N : ℕ, 0 < N ∧ ‖u ^ N - 1‖ < 1 then
    ((Nat.find h : ℕ) : K)⁻¹ * extLogOnePlus (u ^ Nat.find h - 1)
  else 0

variable (p : ℕ) [hp : Fact p.Prime] {K : Type*} [NormedField K] [NormedAlgebra ℚ_[p] K]

include hp

/-- `N⁻¹ log (u ^ N)` does not depend on the exponent `N` with `‖u ^ N - 1‖ < 1`. -/
theorem extLogUnit_aux [CompleteSpace K] {u : K} {M N : ℕ} (hM : 0 < M)
    (hMu : ‖u ^ M - 1‖ < 1) (hN : 0 < N) (hNu : ‖u ^ N - 1‖ < 1) :
    (M : K)⁻¹ * extLogOnePlus (u ^ M - 1) = (N : K)⁻¹ * extLogOnePlus (u ^ N - 1) := by
  have := extLog_charZero p (K := K)
  have e1 := (extLogOnePlus_pow_sub_one p hMu N).2
  have e2 := (extLogOnePlus_pow_sub_one p hNu M).2
  have r1 : (1 + (u ^ M - 1)) ^ N - 1 = u ^ (M * N) - 1 := by
    rw [show 1 + (u ^ M - 1) = u ^ M by ring, ← pow_mul]
  have r2 : (1 + (u ^ N - 1)) ^ M - 1 = u ^ (M * N) - 1 := by
    rw [show 1 + (u ^ N - 1) = u ^ N by ring, ← pow_mul, Nat.mul_comm N M]
  rw [r1] at e1
  rw [r2] at e2
  have hM0 : (M : K) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast hM.ne'
  have hN0 : (N : K) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast hN.ne'
  have key : (N : K) * extLogOnePlus (u ^ M - 1) = (M : K) * extLogOnePlus (u ^ N - 1) :=
    e1.symm.trans e2
  field_simp
  linear_combination key

/-- `log u = N⁻¹ log (u ^ N)` for every `N > 0` with `‖u ^ N - 1‖ < 1`. -/
theorem extLogUnit_eq [CompleteSpace K] {u : K} {N : ℕ} (hN : 0 < N) (hu : ‖u ^ N - 1‖ < 1) :
    extLogUnit u = (N : K)⁻¹ * extLogOnePlus (u ^ N - 1) := by
  have h : ∃ N : ℕ, 0 < N ∧ ‖u ^ N - 1‖ < 1 := ⟨N, hN, hu⟩
  rw [extLogUnit, dite_eq_left h]
  exact extLogUnit_aux p (Nat.find_spec h).1 (Nat.find_spec h).2 hN hu

/-- On principal units, the logarithm of units is the series: `log (1 + x)` for `‖x‖ < 1`. -/
theorem extLogUnit_one_add [CompleteSpace K] {x : K} (hx : ‖x‖ < 1) :
    extLogUnit (1 + x) = extLogOnePlus x := by
  rw [extLogUnit_eq p one_pos (by simpa using hx)]
  simp

/-- `log (u ^ m) = m log u`. -/
theorem extLogUnit_pow [CompleteSpace K] {u : K} {N : ℕ} (hN : 0 < N) (hu : ‖u ^ N - 1‖ < 1)
    (m : ℕ) : extLogUnit (u ^ m) = m * extLogUnit u := by
  have hx := extLogOnePlus_pow_sub_one p hu m
  have r : (1 + (u ^ N - 1)) ^ m - 1 = (u ^ m) ^ N - 1 := by
    rw [show 1 + (u ^ N - 1) = u ^ N by ring, ← pow_mul, ← pow_mul, Nat.mul_comm N m]
  rw [r] at hx
  rw [extLogUnit_eq p hN hx.1, hx.2, extLogUnit_eq p hN hu]
  ring

/-- `log (u v) = log u + log v` when `u ^ N`, `v ^ N` lie in the open disc around `1`. -/
theorem extLogUnit_mul [CompleteSpace K] {u v : K} {N : ℕ} (hN : 0 < N) (hu : ‖u ^ N - 1‖ < 1)
    (hv : ‖v ^ N - 1‖ < 1) : extLogUnit (u * v) = extLogUnit u + extLogUnit v := by
  have := extLog_isUltrametricDist p (K := K)
  have he : (u * v) ^ N - 1 = (u ^ N - 1) + (v ^ N - 1) + (u ^ N - 1) * (v ^ N - 1) := by
    rw [mul_pow]; ring
  have hab : ‖(u * v) ^ N - 1‖ < 1 := by
    rw [he]
    refine (IsUltrametricDist.norm_add_le_max _ _).trans_lt (max_lt ?_ ?_)
    · exact (IsUltrametricDist.norm_add_le_max _ _).trans_lt (max_lt hu hv)
    · rw [norm_mul]; exact (mul_le_of_le_one_right (norm_nonneg _) hv.le).trans_lt hu
  rw [extLogUnit_eq p hN hab, he, extLogOnePlus_add_add_mul p hu hv, extLogUnit_eq p hN hu,
    extLogUnit_eq p hN hv, mul_add]

/-- `‖binom(p, k)‖ ≤ 1 / p` in `K` for `0 < k < p`. -/
theorem extLog_norm_choose_le {k : ℕ} (hk0 : k ≠ 0) (hkp : k < p) :
    ‖((p.choose k : ℕ) : K)‖ ≤ (p : ℝ)⁻¹ := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hp.out.dvd_choose_self hk0 hkp
  rw [extLog_norm_natCast p, hm, Nat.cast_mul, norm_mul, Padic.norm_p]
  have : ‖(m : ℚ_[p])‖ ≤ 1 := by simpa using Padic.norm_int_le_one (p := p) (m : ℤ)
  have h0 : (0 : ℝ) ≤ (p : ℝ)⁻¹ := by positivity
  nlinarith [norm_nonneg (m : ℚ_[p])]

/-- Injectivity of Frobenius on the residue field, analytically: if `‖y‖ ≤ 1` and
`‖y ^ p - 1‖ < 1`, then `‖y - 1‖ < 1`. -/
theorem extLog_norm_sub_one_lt_of_pow {y : K} (hy : ‖y‖ ≤ 1) (h : ‖y ^ p - 1‖ < 1) :
    ‖y - 1‖ < 1 := by
  have := extLog_isUltrametricDist p (K := K)
  have hp1 : (1 : ℝ) < p := by exact_mod_cast hp.out.one_lt
  set t := y - 1 with htdef
  have ht : ‖t‖ ≤ 1 := (extLog_norm_sub_le_max y 1).trans (max_le hy norm_one.le)
  set S := ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (p - 1), t ^ (i + 1) * ((p.choose (i + 1) : ℕ) : K) with hSdef
  have hS : ‖S‖ ≤ (p : ℝ)⁻¹ := by
    refine IsUltrametricDist.norm_sum_le_of_forall_le_of_nonneg (by positivity) fun i hi => ?_
    simp only [Finset.mem_range] at hi
    rw [norm_mul, norm_pow]
    calc ‖t‖ ^ (i + 1) * ‖((p.choose (i + 1) : ℕ) : K)‖ ≤ 1 * (p : ℝ)⁻¹ :=
          mul_le_mul (pow_le_one₀ (norm_nonneg _) ht)
            (extLog_norm_choose_le p (Nat.succ_ne_zero i) (by omega)) (norm_nonneg _) zero_le_one
      _ = (p : ℝ)⁻¹ := one_mul _
  have hsplit : y ^ p - 1 = S + t ^ p := by
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ : ∃ s, p = s + 1 := ⟨p - 1, by have := hp.out.two_le; omega⟩
    have hy' : y = t + 1 := by rw [htdef]; ring
    rw [hSdef, hy', add_pow, hs, Finset.sum_range_succ, Finset.sum_range_succ']
    simp
    ring
  have htp : ‖t ^ p‖ < 1 := by
    have : t ^ p = (y ^ p - 1) - S := by rw [hsplit]; ring
    rw [this]
    exact (extLog_norm_sub_le_max _ _).trans_lt (max_lt h (hS.trans_lt (inv_lt_one_of_one_lt₀ hp1)))
  rw [norm_pow] at htp
  exact (pow_lt_one_iff_of_nonneg (norm_nonneg _) hp.out.ne_zero).mp htp

/-- The least positive `N` with `‖u ^ N - 1‖ < 1` is prime to `p`, for `‖u‖ ≤ 1`. -/
theorem extLog_find_not_dvd {u : K} (hu : ‖u‖ ≤ 1) (h : ∃ N : ℕ, 0 < N ∧ ‖u ^ N - 1‖ < 1) :
    ¬ p ∣ Nat.find h := by
  rintro ⟨M', hM'⟩
  obtain ⟨hpos, hlt⟩ := Nat.find_spec h
  have hM'0 : 0 < M' := by
    rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos M' with h0 | h0
    · rw [h0, mul_zero] at hM'; omega
    · exact h0
  have hy : ‖u ^ M'‖ ≤ 1 := by rw [norm_pow]; exact pow_le_one₀ (norm_nonneg _) hu
  have hyp : ‖(u ^ M') ^ p - 1‖ < 1 := by rw [← pow_mul, Nat.mul_comm M' p, ← hM']; exact hlt
  have h1 := extLog_norm_sub_one_lt_of_pow p hy hyp
  have hlt' : M' < Nat.find h := by rw [hM']; have := hp.out.two_le; nlinarith
  exact Nat.find_min h hlt' ⟨hM'0, h1⟩

/-- For `‖u‖ ≤ 1` some power of which is a principal unit, `‖log u‖ = ‖log (1 + x)‖` for some
`x` in the open unit disc (namely `x = u ^ N - 1` with `N` prime to `p`). -/
theorem extLogUnit_exists_eq [CompleteSpace K] {u : K} (hu : ‖u‖ ≤ 1)
    (h : ∃ N : ℕ, 0 < N ∧ ‖u ^ N - 1‖ < 1) :
    ∃ x : K, ‖x‖ < 1 ∧ ‖extLogUnit u‖ = ‖extLogOnePlus x‖ := by
  obtain ⟨hpos, hlt⟩ := Nat.find_spec h
  refine ⟨u ^ Nat.find h - 1, hlt, ?_⟩
  rw [extLogUnit_eq p hpos hlt, norm_mul, norm_inv, extLog_norm_natCast p,
    Padic.norm_natCast_eq_one_iff.mpr
      ((Nat.Prime.coprime_iff_not_dvd hp.out).mpr (extLog_find_not_dvd p hu h)), inv_one, one_mul]

omit hp in
/-- In a locally compact (proper) normed field, every `u` with `‖u‖ = 1` has a positive power in
the open disc around `1` (the residue field is finite). -/
theorem extLog_exists_pow_near_one [ProperSpace K] {u : K} (hu : ‖u‖ = 1) :
    ∃ N : ℕ, 0 < N ∧ ‖u ^ N - 1‖ < 1 := by
  have hmem : ∀ n : ℕ, u ^ n ∈ Metric.closedBall (0 : K) 1 := fun n => by
    simp [norm_pow, hu]
  obtain ⟨a, -, φ, hφ, hlim⟩ := (isCompact_closedBall (0 : K) 1).tendsto_subseq hmem
  obtain ⟨M, hM⟩ := Metric.cauchySeq_iff'.mp hlim.cauchySeq 1 one_pos
  have h1 := hM (M + 1) (by omega)
  have hlt : φ M < φ (M + 1) := hφ (by omega)
  refine ⟨φ (M + 1) - φ M, Nat.sub_pos_of_lt hlt, ?_⟩
  rw [dist_eq_norm] at h1
  have hsplit : u ^ φ (M + 1) - u ^ φ M = u ^ φ M * (u ^ (φ (M + 1) - φ M) - 1) := by
    rw [mul_sub, mul_one, ← pow_add, Nat.add_sub_cancel' hlt.le]
  simp only [Function.comp_apply] at h1
  rwa [hsplit, norm_mul, norm_pow, hu, one_pow, one_mul] at h1

end Units

section Proposition

variable (p : ℕ) [hp : Fact p.Prime] {K : Type*} [NormedField K] [NormedAlgebra ℚ_[p] K]

include hp

/-- `p ^ (-a)` lies in the disc of the isometry: `p (p ^ (-a)) ^ (p - 1) < 1`, from
`a > 1 / (p - 1)` (`Proposition1_2.a_gt`). -/
theorem extLog_rpow_neg_a_mem_disc {e : ℕ} (he : 1 ≤ e) :
    (p : ℝ) * ((p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p e)) ^ (p - 1) < 1 := by
  have hp0 : (0 : ℝ) < p := by exact_mod_cast hp.out.pos
  have hp1 : (1 : ℝ) < p := by exact_mod_cast hp.out.one_lt
  have ha := Proposition1_2.a_gt hp.out.two_le he
  have hs : ((p - 1 : ℕ) : ℝ) = (p : ℝ) - 1 := by
    rw [Nat.cast_sub hp.out.one_lt.le]; simp
  have hs0 : (0 : ℝ) < (p : ℝ) - 1 := by linarith
  rw [← Real.rpow_natCast, ← Real.rpow_mul hp0.le, hs]
  have hlt : -Proposition1_2.a p e * ((p : ℝ) - 1) < -1 := by
    have := (div_lt_iff₀ hs0).mp ha
    linarith
  calc (p : ℝ) * (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p e * ((p : ℝ) - 1))
      < (p : ℝ) * (p : ℝ) ^ (-1 : ℝ) :=
        mul_lt_mul_of_pos_left (Real.rpow_lt_rpow_of_exponent_lt hp1 hlt) hp0
    _ = 1 := by rw [Real.rpow_neg_one]; field_simp

/-- **IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (i), first inclusion**: `p ^ a · R ⊆ log (R^×)`, with `R` the closed
unit ball, `R^×` the unit sphere, `p ^ a · R = {z | ‖z‖ ≤ p ^ (-a)}` and `a = a_i` of page 10.
Valid for every `e ≥ 1`. -/
theorem extLogUnit_image_lower [CompleteSpace K] {e : ℕ} (he : 1 ≤ e) :
    {z : K | ‖z‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p e)} ⊆ extLogUnit '' {u : K | ‖u‖ = 1} := by
  have := extLog_isUltrametricDist p (K := K)
  intro z hz
  have hr0 : (0 : ℝ) ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p e) := Real.rpow_nonneg (by positivity) _
  have hpr := extLog_rpow_neg_a_mem_disc p he
  obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := extLogOnePlus_surjOn p hr0 hpr hz
  have hx1 : ‖x‖ < 1 := hx.trans_lt (extLog_lt_one_of_mul_pow_lt_one hp.out.one_lt.le hpr)
  exact ⟨1 + x, extLog_norm_one_add hx1, extLogUnit_one_add p hx1⟩

/-- With `c = ⌊log (p e / (p - 1)) / log p⌋ ≥ 0`: `e < p ^ (c + 1)` (from
`Proposition1_2.rpow_b_gt`) and `p ^ b = p ^ c · p ^ (-1 / e)`. -/
theorem extLog_b_facts {e : ℕ} (he : 1 ≤ e) :
    ∃ c : ℕ, e < p ^ (c + 1) ∧
      (p : ℝ) ^ (Proposition1_2.b p e) = (p : ℝ) ^ c * (p : ℝ) ^ (-(1 / (e : ℝ))) := by
  have hp0 : (0 : ℝ) < p := by exact_mod_cast hp.out.pos
  have hp2 : (2 : ℝ) ≤ p := by exact_mod_cast hp.out.two_le
  have he' : (1 : ℝ) ≤ e := by exact_mod_cast he
  set F := ⌊Real.log ((p : ℝ) * e / ((p : ℝ) - 1)) / Real.log p⌋ with hF
  have hF0 : 0 ≤ F := by
    apply Int.floor_nonneg.mpr
    apply div_nonneg (Real.log_nonneg ?_) (Real.log_nonneg (by linarith))
    rw [le_div_iff₀ (by linarith)]; nlinarith
  have hFn : ((F.toNat : ℕ) : ℝ) = (F : ℝ) := by exact_mod_cast Int.toNat_of_nonneg hF0
  refine ⟨F.toNat, ?_, ?_⟩
  · have hg := Proposition1_2.rpow_b_gt hp.out.two_le he
    rw [Proposition1_2.b_add_inv, ← hF, ← hFn, Real.rpow_natCast] at hg
    have h1 : (e : ℝ) < ((p : ℝ) - 1) * (p : ℝ) ^ F.toNat := by
      rw [div_lt_div_iff₀ (by linarith) (by linarith)] at hg; linarith
    have h2 : ((p : ℝ) - 1) * (p : ℝ) ^ F.toNat < (p : ℝ) ^ (F.toNat + 1) := by
      rw [pow_succ]; nlinarith [pow_pos hp0 F.toNat]
    exact_mod_cast h1.trans h2
  · rw [← Real.rpow_natCast, ← Real.rpow_add hp0, hFn]
    congr 1

/-- The termwise estimate for the second inclusion: if `e < p ^ (c + 1)`, `0 ≤ ρ ≤ 1`,
`ρ ^ e = 1 / p` and `‖x‖ ≤ ρ`, then `‖x ^ n / n‖ ≤ p ^ c ρ` for every `n`. -/
theorem extLogSeries_norm_le_upper {e c : ℕ} (he : e < p ^ (c + 1)) {ρ : ℝ} (hρ0 : 0 ≤ ρ)
    (hρ1 : ρ ≤ 1) (hρe : ρ ^ e = (p : ℝ)⁻¹) {x : K} (hx : ‖x‖ ≤ ρ) (n : ℕ) :
    ‖extLogSeries x n‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ c * ρ := by
  have hp0 : (0 : ℝ) < p := by exact_mod_cast hp.out.pos
  have hp1 : (1 : ℝ) ≤ p := by exact_mod_cast hp.out.one_lt.le
  rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos n with rfl | hn
  · simp only [extLogSeries, Nat.cast_zero, div_zero, zero_mul, norm_zero]
    exact mul_nonneg (by positivity) hρ0
  obtain ⟨v, hdvd, hv⟩ := padicLog_exists_norm_inv_natCast (p := p) (n := n) hn.ne'
  rw [extLogSeries, div_eq_mul_inv, norm_mul, norm_mul, norm_pow, norm_neg, norm_one, one_pow,
    one_mul, norm_pow, norm_inv, extLog_norm_natCast p, ← norm_inv, hv]
  have hpv : p ^ v ≤ n := Nat.le_of_dvd hn hdvd
  have harith := extLog_val_arith hp.out.two_le hn hpv he
  obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ : ∃ m, n = m + 1 := ⟨n - 1, by omega⟩
  simp only [Nat.add_sub_cancel] at harith
  have hxn : ‖x‖ ^ (m + 1) ≤ ρ ^ (m + 1) := pow_le_pow_left₀ (norm_nonneg _) hx _
  refine (mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hxn (by positivity)).trans ?_
  rw [pow_succ]
  rcases le_or_gt v c with hvc | hvc
  · calc (p : ℝ) ^ v * (ρ ^ m * ρ) ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ c * (1 * ρ) :=
          mul_le_mul (pow_le_pow_right₀ hp1 hvc)
            (mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (pow_le_one₀ hρ0 hρ1) hρ0)
            (mul_nonneg (pow_nonneg hρ0 _) hρ0) (by positivity)
      _ = (p : ℝ) ^ c * ρ := by ring
  · obtain ⟨d, rfl⟩ : ∃ d, v = c + d := ⟨v - c, by omega⟩
    have hde : d * e ≤ m := Nat.le_of_add_le_add_left (by rwa [add_mul] at harith)
    have h1 : ρ ^ m ≤ ρ ^ (d * e) := pow_le_pow_of_le_one hρ0 hρ1 hde
    have h2 : ρ ^ (d * e) = ((p : ℝ)⁻¹) ^ d := by rw [mul_comm, pow_mul, hρe]
    calc (p : ℝ) ^ (c + d) * (ρ ^ m * ρ) ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (c + d) * (((p : ℝ)⁻¹) ^ d * ρ) := by
          rw [← h2]
          exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right h1 hρ0) (by positivity)
      _ = (p : ℝ) ^ c * ρ := by
          rw [pow_add, inv_pow]
          field_simp

/-- **IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (i), second inclusion**: `log (R^×) ⊆ p ^ (-b) · R`, with
`p ^ (-b) · R = {z | ‖z‖ ≤ p ^ b}` and `b = b_i` of page 10, for a locally compact `K` in which
every element of the open unit disc has norm at most `p ^ (-1 / e)` (this holds when `e` is the
ramification index: the value group is then `p ^ (ℤ / e)`). -/
theorem extLogUnit_image_upper [CompleteSpace K] [ProperSpace K] {e : ℕ} (he : 1 ≤ e)
    (hval : ∀ x : K, ‖x‖ < 1 → ‖x‖ ^ e ≤ (p : ℝ)⁻¹) :
    extLogUnit '' {u : K | ‖u‖ = 1} ⊆ {z : K | ‖z‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (Proposition1_2.b p e)} := by
  have := extLog_isUltrametricDist p (K := K)
  rintro _ ⟨u, hu, rfl⟩
  have hu' : ‖u‖ = 1 := hu
  obtain ⟨c, hce, hb⟩ := extLog_b_facts p he
  have hp0 : (0 : ℝ) < p := by exact_mod_cast hp.out.pos
  have hp1 : (1 : ℝ) ≤ p := by exact_mod_cast hp.out.one_lt.le
  have he0 : (e : ℝ) ≠ 0 := Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr (by omega)
  set ρ : ℝ := (p : ℝ) ^ (-(1 / (e : ℝ))) with hρdef
  have hρ0 : 0 ≤ ρ := Real.rpow_nonneg hp0.le _
  have hρe : ρ ^ e = (p : ℝ)⁻¹ := by
    rw [hρdef, ← Real.rpow_natCast, ← Real.rpow_mul hp0.le,
      show -(1 / (e : ℝ)) * (e : ℝ) = -1 by field_simp]
    exact Real.rpow_neg_one _
  have hρ1 : ρ ≤ 1 := by
    refine Real.rpow_le_one_of_one_le_of_nonpos hp1 ?_
    have : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 1 / (e : ℝ) := by positivity
    linarith
  obtain ⟨x, hx1, hnorm⟩ := extLogUnit_exists_eq p hu'.le (extLog_exists_pow_near_one hu')
  have hxρ : ‖x‖ ≤ ρ := by
    have := hval x hx1
    rw [← hρe] at this
    exact (pow_le_pow_iff_left₀ (norm_nonneg _) hρ0 (by omega)).mp this
  show ‖extLogUnit u‖ ≤ _
  rw [hnorm, hb, extLogOnePlus]
  exact IsUltrametricDist.norm_tsum_le_of_forall_le_of_nonneg
    (mul_nonneg (by positivity) hρ0) fun n => extLogSeries_norm_le_upper p hce hρ0 hρ1 hρe hxρ n

/-- **IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (i)** (page 10), both inclusions
`p ^ (a_i) · R_i ⊆ log (R_i^×) ⊆ p ^ (-b_i) · R_i`, for a complete, locally compact normed field
`K` that is a normed `ℚ_p`-algebra, with `R` the closed unit ball, `R^×` the unit sphere,
`p ^ λ · R = {z | ‖z‖ ≤ p ^ (-λ)}`, `log` on `R^×` the function `extLogUnit`, and `e` a
positive integer such that the open unit disc lies in the closed disc of radius `p ^ (-1 / e)`. -/
theorem extLogUnit_image_bounds [CompleteSpace K] [ProperSpace K] {e : ℕ} (he : 1 ≤ e)
    (hval : ∀ x : K, ‖x‖ < 1 → ‖x‖ ^ e ≤ (p : ℝ)⁻¹) :
    {z : K | ‖z‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p e)} ⊆ extLogUnit '' {u : K | ‖u‖ = 1} ∧
      extLogUnit '' {u : K | ‖u‖ = 1} ⊆ {z : K | ‖z‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (Proposition1_2.b p e)} :=
  ⟨extLogUnit_image_lower p he, extLogUnit_image_upper p he hval⟩

/-- **IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (i), the equality case**: for `p > 2` and `e ≤ p - 2`,
`log (R^×) = p ^ (1 / e) · R = {z | ‖z‖ ≤ p ^ (-1 / e)}` (here `a_i = 1 / e_i = -b_i`,
`Proposition1_2.a_b_of_le`). -/
theorem extLogUnit_image_eq_of_le [CompleteSpace K] [ProperSpace K] {e : ℕ} (he : 1 ≤ e)
    (hp2 : 2 < p) (hep : e ≤ p - 2) (hval : ∀ x : K, ‖x‖ < 1 → ‖x‖ ^ e ≤ (p : ℝ)⁻¹) :
    extLogUnit '' {u : K | ‖u‖ = 1} = {z : K | ‖z‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (-(1 / (e : ℝ)))} := by
  obtain ⟨ha, hb⟩ := Proposition1_2.a_b_of_le hp2 he hep
  have h := extLogUnit_image_bounds p he hval
  rw [ha, hb] at h
  exact Set.Subset.antisymm h.2 h.1

/-- **The unramified case** `e = 1`, `p > 2`: `log (R^×) = p · R = {z | ‖z‖ ≤ 1 / p}`. -/
theorem extLogUnit_image_unramified [CompleteSpace K] [ProperSpace K] (hp2 : 2 < p)
    (hval : ∀ x : K, ‖x‖ < 1 → ‖x‖ ≤ (p : ℝ)⁻¹) :
    extLogUnit '' {u : K | ‖u‖ = 1} = {z : K | ‖z‖ ≤ (p : ℝ)⁻¹} := by
  rw [extLogUnit_image_eq_of_le p le_rfl hp2 (by omega) (fun x hx => by simpa using hval x hx)]
  simp [Real.rpow_neg_one]

/-- The same inclusions for a finite extension `L` of `ℚ_p` carrying a norm that extends the
`p`-adic norm (completeness and local compactness follow from finite dimensionality). -/
theorem extLogUnit_image_bounds_of_finiteDimensional {L : Type*} [NormedField L]
    [NormedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L] [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] L] {e : ℕ} (he : 1 ≤ e)
    (hval : ∀ x : L, ‖x‖ < 1 → ‖x‖ ^ e ≤ (p : ℝ)⁻¹) :
    {z : L | ‖z‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p e)} ⊆ extLogUnit '' {u : L | ‖u‖ = 1} ∧
      extLogUnit '' {u : L | ‖u‖ = 1} ⊆ {z : L | ‖z‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (Proposition1_2.b p e)} := by
  have : CompleteSpace L := FiniteDimensional.completeSpace ℚ_[p] L
  have : ProperSpace L := FiniteDimensional.proper ℚ_[p] L
  exact extLogUnit_image_bounds p he hval

end Proposition

section BaseField

variable (p : ℕ) [hp : Fact p.Prime]

/-- Over `ℚ_p` the series is that of `IUT.Prerequisites.PadicLog`. -/
theorem extLogOnePlus_padic (x : ℚ_[p]) : extLogOnePlus x = padicLogOnePlus p x := rfl

/-- Over `ℚ_p`, on `ℤ_p^×`, the logarithm of units is `padicLogUnit` of
`IUT.Prerequisites.PadicLog`. -/
theorem extLogUnit_padic (u : ℤ_[p]ˣ) :
    extLogUnit ((u : ℤ_[p]) : ℚ_[p]) = padicLogUnit p ((u : ℤ_[p]) : ℚ_[p]) := by
  have hρ : (p : ℝ)⁻¹ < 1 := inv_lt_one_of_one_lt₀ (by exact_mod_cast hp.out.one_lt)
  have h := (padicLog_norm_pow_sub_one_le u).trans_lt hρ
  rw [extLogUnit_eq p (by have := hp.out.two_le; omega : 0 < p - 1) h, padicLogUnit]
  rfl

/-- In `ℚ_p` the open unit disc lies in the closed disc of radius `1 / p` (`e = 1`). -/
theorem extLog_padic_disc (x : ℚ_[p]) (hx : ‖x‖ < 1) : ‖x‖ ≤ (p : ℝ)⁻¹ := by
  have := (Padic.norm_le_pow_iff_norm_lt_pow_add_one x (-1)).mpr (by simpa using hx)
  simpa [zpow_neg] using this

/-- **Consistency with the base field** (`a = 1`, `b = -1` for odd `p`): for `K = ℚ_p` the
image `log (R^×)` given by `extLogUnit_image_unramified` is the image `log (ℤ_p^×)` of
`IUT.Prerequisites.PadicLog.padicLogUnit_range_of_ne_two`. -/
theorem extLogUnit_image_padic_of_ne_two (h2 : p ≠ 2) :
    extLogUnit '' {u : ℚ_[p] | ‖u‖ = 1} =
      Set.range (fun u : ℤ_[p]ˣ => padicLogUnit p ((u : ℤ_[p]) : ℚ_[p])) := by
  have hp2 : 2 < p := lt_of_le_of_ne hp.out.two_le (Ne.symm h2)
  rw [extLogUnit_image_unramified p hp2 (extLog_padic_disc p), padicLogUnit_range_of_ne_two h2]

end BaseField

section LogShell

/-- The log-shell of IUT III Definition 1.1 (page 24) for a normed field `K`:
`I = (p*)⁻¹ · log (R^×)`, with `R^×` the unit sphere and `p* = p` for odd `p`, `p* = 4` for
`p = 2`. -/
noncomputable def extLogShell (p : ℕ) (K : Type*) [NormedField K] : Set K :=
  (fun z => ((padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : K)⁻¹ * z) '' (extLogUnit '' {u : K | ‖u‖ = 1})

variable (p : ℕ) [hp : Fact p.Prime] {K : Type*} [NormedField K] [NormedAlgebra ℚ_[p] K]

include hp

/-- `‖p*‖ = 1 / p*` in `K`. -/
theorem extLog_norm_pStar : ‖((padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : K)‖ = ((padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : ℝ)⁻¹ := by
  rw [extLog_norm_natCast p]; exact padicLog_norm_pStar

/-- `y ∈ I` if and only if `p* y ∈ log (R^×)`. -/
theorem extLogShell_mem_iff {y : K} :
    y ∈ extLogShell p K ↔ ((padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : K) * y ∈ extLogUnit '' {u : K | ‖u‖ = 1} := by
  have hpos : (0 : ℝ) < ((padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : ℝ) := by
    exact_mod_cast lt_of_lt_of_le hp.out.pos padicLog_pStar_ge
  have hs0 : ((padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : K) ≠ 0 := by
    rw [← norm_pos_iff, extLog_norm_pStar p]; exact inv_pos.mpr hpos
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩
    rwa [← mul_assoc, mul_inv_cancel₀ hs0, one_mul]
  · intro h
    exact ⟨_, h, by dsimp only; rw [← mul_assoc, inv_mul_cancel₀ hs0, one_mul]⟩

/-- `1 / p* ≤ p ^ (-a)`: `a ≤ 1` for odd `p`, and `a = 2`, `p* = 4` for `p = 2`. -/
theorem extLog_inv_pStar_le_rpow_neg_a {e : ℕ} (he : 1 ≤ e) :
    ((padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : ℝ)⁻¹ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p e) := by
  by_cases h2 : p = 2
  · subst h2
    have ha : Proposition1_2.a 2 e = 2 := by simp [Proposition1_2.a]
    rw [ha, show (-(2 : ℝ)) = ((-2 : ℤ) : ℝ) by norm_num, Real.rpow_intCast]
    simp [padicLogPStar]
    norm_num
  · have hp1 : (1 : ℝ) ≤ p := by exact_mod_cast hp.out.one_lt.le
    have hp3 : (3 : ℝ) ≤ p := by
      have : 2 < p := lt_of_le_of_ne hp.out.two_le (Ne.symm h2)
      exact_mod_cast this
    have he' : (1 : ℝ) ≤ e := by exact_mod_cast he
    have ha1 : Proposition1_2.a p e ≤ 1 := by
      simp only [Proposition1_2.a, h2, ite_false]
      have hc : (⌈(e : ℝ) / ((p : ℝ) - 2)⌉ : ℝ) ≤ e := by
        have : ⌈(e : ℝ) / ((p : ℝ) - 2)⌉ ≤ (e : ℤ) := by
          rw [Int.ceil_le]; push_cast
          rw [div_le_iff₀ (by linarith)]; nlinarith
        exact_mod_cast this
      calc 1 / (e : ℝ) * ⌈(e : ℝ) / ((p : ℝ) - 2)⌉ ≤ 1 / (e : ℝ) * e :=
            mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hc (by positivity)
        _ = 1 := by field_simp
    simp only [padicLogPStar, h2, ite_false]
    rw [← Real.rpow_neg_one]
    exact Real.rpow_le_rpow_of_exponent_le hp1 (by linarith)

/-- **IUT III Proposition 1.2 (v) (b_non)** (page 32) for `K`: the log-shell contains the closed
unit ball `R`. -/
theorem extLogShell_unitBall_subset [CompleteSpace K] : {y : K | ‖y‖ ≤ 1} ⊆ extLogShell p K := by
  intro y hy
  have hy' : ‖y‖ ≤ 1 := hy
  rw [extLogShell_mem_iff p]
  refine extLogUnit_image_lower p (e := 1) le_rfl ?_
  show ‖((padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : K) * y‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p 1)
  rw [norm_mul, extLog_norm_pStar p]
  calc ((padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : ℝ)⁻¹ * ‖y‖ ≤ ((padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : ℝ)⁻¹ * 1 :=
        mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hy' (by positivity)
    _ ≤ _ := by rw [mul_one]; exact extLog_inv_pStar_le_rpow_neg_a p le_rfl

/-- **IUT III Proposition 1.2 (v) (c_non)** (page 32) for a locally compact `K`: the log-shell
contains `log (R^×)`. -/
theorem extLogUnit_image_subset_extLogShell [CompleteSpace K] [ProperSpace K] :
    extLogUnit '' {u : K | ‖u‖ = 1} ⊆ extLogShell p K := by
  rintro _ ⟨u, hu, rfl⟩
  have hu' : ‖u‖ = 1 := hu
  rw [extLogShell_mem_iff p]
  obtain ⟨N, hN, hNu⟩ := extLog_exists_pow_near_one hu'
  refine ⟨u ^ padicLogPStar p, by simp [norm_pow, hu'], ?_⟩
  exact extLogUnit_pow p hN hNu _

/-- The bounds on the log-shell given by IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (i):
`p* p ^ a · R ⊆ I ⊆ p* p ^ (-b) · R`, written with closed balls of radii `p* p ^ (-a)` and
`p* p ^ b`. -/
theorem extLogShell_bounds [CompleteSpace K] [ProperSpace K] {e : ℕ} (he : 1 ≤ e)
    (hval : ∀ x : K, ‖x‖ < 1 → ‖x‖ ^ e ≤ (p : ℝ)⁻¹) :
    {y : K | ‖y‖ ≤ ((padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : ℝ) * (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p e)} ⊆
        extLogShell p K ∧
      extLogShell p K ⊆
        {y : K | ‖y‖ ≤ ((padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : ℝ) * (p : ℝ) ^ (Proposition1_2.b p e)} := by
  have hS : (0 : ℝ) < ((padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : ℝ) := by
    exact_mod_cast lt_of_lt_of_le hp.out.pos padicLog_pStar_ge
  constructor
  · intro y hy
    have hy' : ‖y‖ ≤ ((padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : ℝ) * (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p e) := hy
    rw [extLogShell_mem_iff p]
    refine extLogUnit_image_lower p he ?_
    show ‖((padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : K) * y‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p e)
    rw [norm_mul, extLog_norm_pStar p, inv_mul_le_iff₀ hS]
    exact hy'
  · intro y hy
    rw [extLogShell_mem_iff p] at hy
    have h := extLogUnit_image_upper p he hval hy
    have h' : ‖((padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : K) * y‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (Proposition1_2.b p e) := h
    rw [norm_mul, extLog_norm_pStar p, inv_mul_le_iff₀ hS] at h'
    exact h'

end LogShell

section SpectralNorm

/-! A finite extension `L` of `ℚ_p` given only by the classes of `IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields.Padic`
(a field with a finite-dimensional `ℚ_p`-algebra structure), equipped with Mathlib's spectral
norm `spectralNorm ℚ_[p] L`, the norm extending the `p`-adic norm. -/

variable (p : ℕ) [hp : Fact p.Prime] (L : Type*) [Field L] [Algebra ℚ_[p] L]
  [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] L]

include hp

/-- **IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (i)** for a finite extension `L` of `ℚ_p` with its spectral norm:
`p ^ a · R ⊆ log (R^×) ⊆ p ^ (-b) · R` in the closed-ball model, the second inclusion for every
`e ≥ 1` such that the open unit disc of `L` lies in the closed disc of radius `p ^ (-1 / e)`. -/
theorem extLogUnit_image_bounds_spectralNorm {e : ℕ} (he : 1 ≤ e)
    (hval : letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
      ∀ x : L, ‖x‖ < 1 → ‖x‖ ^ e ≤ (p : ℝ)⁻¹) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    {z : L | ‖z‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p e)} ⊆ extLogUnit '' {u : L | ‖u‖ = 1} ∧
      extLogUnit '' {u : L | ‖u‖ = 1} ⊆ {z : L | ‖z‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (Proposition1_2.b p e)} := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  let := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
  exact extLogUnit_image_bounds_of_finiteDimensional p he hval

/-- The first inclusion `p ^ a · R ⊆ log (R^×)` and IUT III Proposition 1.2 (v) (b_non),
`R ⊆ I`, for a finite extension `L` of `ℚ_p` with its spectral norm, for every `e ≥ 1`. -/
theorem extLogUnit_lower_and_shell_spectralNorm {e : ℕ} (he : 1 ≤ e) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    {z : L | ‖z‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p e)} ⊆ extLogUnit '' {u : L | ‖u‖ = 1} ∧
      {y : L | ‖y‖ ≤ 1} ⊆ extLogShell p L := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  let := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
  have : CompleteSpace L := FiniteDimensional.completeSpace ℚ_[p] L
  exact ⟨extLogUnit_image_lower p he, extLogShell_unitBall_subset p⟩

end SpectralNorm

end IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields
